---
import Container from "@moesegfault/style/astro/Container.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout title="Integration guides" description="Integrate MoeSegFault Style into React, Astro, or a no-build web page." currentPath="/en/guides/" locale="en">
  <header class="page-intro"><Container><p class="kicker">GUIDES</p><h1>Start with one line of CSS.</h1><p class="lede">Choose the entry point that fits your project. No React means no React download; tokens alone do not pull in component styles.</p></Container></header>
  <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="install-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Install</p><h2 id="install-title">Package-manager setup</h2></div></div><CodeBlock label="Terminal" code="pnpm add @moesegfault/style" /><div class="guide-grid">
    <article class="guide-card"><h3>React / TypeScript</h3><p>Install <code>react</code> and <code>react-dom</code> 19+ first, load the CSS once at the application entry, then import components as needed.</p><CodeBlock label="src/App.tsx" code={`import "@moesegfault/style/all.css";\nimport { Button, Notice } from "@moesegfault/style/react";\n\nexport function App() {\n  return <Notice title="Hello"><Button>Continue</Button></Notice>;\n}`} /></article>
    <article class="guide-card"><h3>Astro</h3><p>Astro components emit static HTML by default and require no client-side JavaScript.</p><CodeBlock label="src/pages/index.astro" code={`---\nimport "@moesegfault/style/all.css";\nimport Button from "@moesegfault/style/astro/Button.astro";\nimport Card from "@moesegfault/style/astro/Card.astro";\n---\n<Card><h2>Static first</h2><Button href="/start">Start</Button></Card>`} /></article>
    <article class="guide-card"><h3>Astro + React island</h3><p>Add a client directive only to components that truly require interactivity.</p><CodeBlock label="src/pages/chat.astro" code={`---\nimport { Composer } from "../components/Composer";\n---\n<Composer client:visible />`} /></article>
    <article class="guide-card"><h3>Layered CSS</h3><p>The all-in-one entry is easiest; size-sensitive applications can select layers explicitly.</p><CodeBlock label="src/styles/app.css" code={`@import "@moesegfault/style/tokens.css";\n@import "@moesegfault/style/foundation.css";\n@import "@moesegfault/style/components.css";`} /></article>
  </div></Container></section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cdn-title"><Container><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">No build</p><h2 id="cdn-title">Remote assets / native HTML</h2></div><p>Pin a version in production. Default aliases suit prototypes, documentation previews, or controlled automatic updates.</p></div><CodeBlock label="index.html" code={`<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en">\n  <head>\n    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://style.moesegfault.dev/v0.1.1/css/all.css">\n  </head>\n  <body class="moe-surface">\n    <button class="moe-button">Start creating</button>\n  </body>\n</html>`} /><div class="callout"><h3>Theme initialization</h3><p>Set <code>data-moe-theme</code> before first-paint style calculation to avoid a theme flash; this documentation site uses that approach.</p></div></Container></section>
</DocsLayout>
